{"parentUuid":"911e7432-b45b-4b75-9567-dbde6ef568b9","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"0e75e1c2-9f84-43c4-8006-cccad7102c77","agentId":"ab095323a3b740c00","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01UmqUzsDajWNohmboi6GNeP","type":"tool_result","content":"the following rules refused this work:\n  - The compact-nohooks run's boundary has no preservedSegment or preservedMessages, a logicalParentUuid that is the last written record, and postTokens and cumulativeDroppedTokens in compactMetadata. Only TestT017_07c_C\nompactionWithoutAPreservedSegment in test_017_compaction_test.go checks that shape, and it has no `// sr:proves compaction-transcript-continuity/claude` marker, so no marked test covers that recorded variant. The marked \ntests (07, 07d, 07j) only drive the preserved-segment shape.\n  - In the recorded `compact` run (events.jsonl lines 20-21 and 24-25) PreCompact and the later compaction hooks stream `hook_started`/`hook_response` frames around the `status` frames. No listed test asserts those frame\ns when a compaction hook is configured: 07j runs with no hooks, 07k asserts only that they are absent, and the hook-driven tests (07, 07h) check payloads and transcript records but not stream frames. Every other checklis\nt item I traced has a test: PreCompact and PostCompact payload fields with a null `custom_instructions`; the order PreCompact, SubagentStop, SessionStart:compact, PostCompact; exit-2 and JSON-decision blocking; the manua\nl-only stderr message; discarded `continue` and `systemMessage`; manual/auto matchers; a blocked compaction letting the session go on; and the status, init and boundary stream frames.\n  - The doc says a fork at the depth limit keeps the Agent tool but its dispatch returns an error instead of spawning. No test covers this: TestT009_20 only asserts the withheld-tool \"No such tool available: Agent\" case \nfor ordinary sub-agents. The spec declares no deviation for forks, so this documented limit variant is unchecked.\n  - Two recorded behaviours have no test. (1) The recorded fork hook payloads carry the fork new session_id (…b2), but T017_08/T017_09 only collect `source` values and never assert session_id on any hook payload. (2) Run \nthen/03 passes --fork-session --session-id c3 with no --resume, and the real harness fired SessionStart source startup (no fork); no listed test covers this. Also no test resumes the original after forking (then/04, sour\nce resume under the original id); tests only byte-compare the original file.\n  - The headless#continue-conversations doc states `--continue` resumes the most recent conversation and `--resume` accepts the absolute path to a session .jsonl transcript. No test drives either variant, the mock has no\n `--continue` handling, and no deviation declares them unmodeled. By-id resume, cross-directory resume, SessionStart source=resume with no sub-agent hooks, and the resume-fact fields are covered by T004_01, T015_02 to T0\n15_04, T017_06 and T017_31.\n  - The docs state subagents/ transcripts are deleted with the parent session after cleanupPeriodDays (claude-directory 'Cleaned up automatically' table, sub-agents 'Automatic cleanup') and are unaffected by main-convers\nation compaction or session resume, yet no test sets cleanupPeriodDays or checks a sub-agent file surviving compaction/resume, and no deviation declares these behaviours unmodeled.\n30:sloprail: file-guard \"capability-rigor\" manual-compaction: refused (14/23 settled, 2m40s)\n37:sloprail: file-guard \"capability-rigor\" nested-subagents: refused (16/23 settled, 3m2s)\n40:sloprail: file-guard \"capability-rigor\" session-fork: refused (17/23 settled, 3m6s)\n43:sloprail: file-guard \"capability-rigor\" compaction-transcript-continuity: refused (18/23 settled, 3m13s)\n48:sloprail: file-guard \"capability-rigor\" session-resume: refused (20/23 settled, 3m32s)\n52:sloprail: file-guard \"capability-rigor\" subagent-transcripts: refused (22/23 settled, 3m42s)\n79:the following rules refused this work:","is_error":false}]},"uuid":"0a089fc1-8733-44fc-9a73-899f31ee60fb","timestamp":"2026-10-03T18:32:21.226Z","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"911e7432-b45b-4b75-9567-dbde6ef568b9","userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-desktop","cwd":"/Users/nsviridenko/ws/sloprail/harness-mocks/.claude/worktrees/agent-ab095323a3b740c00","sessionId":"f103aecd-8ff6-40a5-ad21-f5bd02338666","version":"2.1.286","gitBranch":"worktree-agent-adc1470310079e23b"}
