-f5bd02338666","version":"2.1.286","gitBranch":"worktree-agent-adc1470310079e23b"}
{"parentUuid":"7dbc8d77-cb1a-4eb3-8c2e-5cd3ecf26cd6","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"0e75e1c2-9f84-43c4-8006-cccad7102c77","agentId":"ab095323a3b740c00","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01Nd4RM9X7rUy4i5Q84x3GgE","type":"tool_result","content":"313:| `background` | No | Set to `true` to keep this subagent in the background even when Claude asks to run it in the foreground. Where [fork mode](#turn-fork-mode-on-or-off) is on, Claude Code already runs the subagents Claude spawns [in the background](#run-subagents-in-foreground-or-background) \n893:* If an in-process [agent team](/docs/en/agent-teams#limitations) teammate spawned the subagent, Claude Code runs it in the foreground. Claude Code refuses with an error to spawn a teammate's subagent whose definition sets [`background: true`](#supported-frontmatter-fields). Where [fork mode](#t\n894:* If you set [`CLAUDE_CODE_DISABLE_BACKGROUND_TASKS`](/docs/en/env-vars) to `1`, Claude Code runs the subagent in the foreground, in every kind of session and whether or not fork mode is on.\n895:* Where [fork mode](#turn-fork-mode-on-or-off) is on, as it is by default in an interactive session, Claude Code runs the subagent in the background, forks and non-fork subagents alike, and Claude can't ask for the foreground.\n896:* Where fork mode is off, Claude runs the subagent in the background by default and in the foreground when it needs the result before continuing. Fork mode is off in [non-interactive mode](/docs/en/headless) with `-p` and in the Agent SDK unless you turn it on. To keep a particular subagent in t\n898:For a skill with `context: fork`, Claude Code follows the rules in [Run skills in a subagent](/docs/en/skills#run-skills-in-a-subagent) instead, whether or not fork mode is on.\n910:* Where fork mode is off, ask Claude to run a task in the background or in the foreground\n1149:Claude starts a fork by requesting the `fork` subagent type through the Agent tool. You control whether it can with [fork mode](#turn-fork-mode-on-or-off), which is on by default in interactive sessions.\n1151:You can start a fork yourself with `/subtask` followed by a task, whether or not fork mode is on. On v2.1.161 through v2.1.211 the command is `/fork`. Claude Code names the fork from the first words of the task. The following example forks the conversation to draft test cases while you continue\n1192:### Turn fork mode on or off","is_error":false}]},"uuid":"4bac1a73-99e0-4d95-9a0f-914d899dd6d6","timestamp":"2026-10-03T18:37:10.542Z","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"7dbc8d77-cb1a-4eb3-8c2e-5cd3ecf26cd6","userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-desktop","cwd":"/Users/nsviridenko/ws/sloprail/harness-mocks/.claude/worktrees/agent-ab095323a3b740c00","sessionId":"f103aecd-8ff6-40a5-ad21-f5bd02338666","version":"2.1.286","gitBranch":"worktree-agent-adc1470310079e23b"}
