runs stream hook_started/hook_response then system/init first (stops also has a 'notification' event), but no test asserts the mock emits those fr\names in that order, because T001_01 and T001_07 get init from their own script. The headless doc's non-zero exit on a failed run and its --output-format text/json modes have no test and no deviation. T001_01 also passes through sc\nript-supplied frames without any recorded sample pinning that shape.\n  - Every listed fork test passes an explicit --session-id for the fork, so none covers the documented core behaviour that --resume --fork-session without --session-id gives the fork its own new id, different from the original, in\n hooks and in the stream init frame (SDK docs: forkedId from init message session_id). Also, the recorded-sequence test checks only hook source and id for the fork and never asserts that the fork transcript carries the recorded hi\nstory (echo ORIGINAL turn).\n  - TestT017_31 (claude-mock/e2e/017_session_lifecycle/test_017_resume_payload_test.go) pins the resume SessionStart context_tokens and estimated_cache_write_usd to 0, but every recorded resume shows non-zero values (e.g. resume-c\nontinue context_tokens 31471, estimated_cache_write_usd 0.0629) and no deviation declares this. The documented `--resume <name>` / `--name` resume-by-name variant (CLI reference --resume and --name rows) is neither tested nor decl\nared a deviation, so it is an uncovered item; the mock has no --name handling.\n  - Code outside the module map (adr/modules-cover-code):\n- claude-mock/internal/runner/session_target.go belongs to no module: put it in a module's home, or add a module.yaml for it\n- claude-mock/session_flags.go belongs to no module: put it in a module's home, or add a module.yaml for it (file-guard \"module-coverage\")","is_error":false}]},"uuid":"8f242adc-812f-4514-b875-3328d2e52282","timestamp":"2026-10-03T18:51:23.009Z","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"d0a67077-45db-42c6-b426-8effb4be9b7d","userType":"exte