{"parentUuid":"99ff2748-7a1f-4671-b08a-2a73a85f4d64","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"0e75e1c2-9f84-43c4-8006-cccad7102c77","agentId":"ab095323a3b740c00","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01NKU2sskJUQpn99zddErmhK","type":"tool_result","content":"statement: >-\n  A sub-agent can itself dispatch sub-agents; each records its depth and its\n  parent, and all of a session's sub-agent transcripts sit in one directory.\n  Nesting stops at a depth limit (three layers by default, set by\n  CLAUDE_CODE_MAX_SUBAGENT_SPAWN_DEPTH), where a dispatch is an error, and in\n  non-interactive mode a sub-agent does not wait for the background sub-agents\n  it launched.\nproviders:\n  claude:\n    docs:\n      - https://code.claude.com/docs/en/sub-agents#let-subagents-spawn-their-own-subagents\n    runs:\n      - claude-mock/snapshots/runs/meta\n<<<<<<< HEAD\n  codex:\n    docs:\n      - https://developers.openai.com/codex/hooks#common-input-fields\n    runs:\n      - codex-mock/snapshots/runs/nested-subagents\n      - codex-mock/snapshots/runs/nested-subagents-limit\n      - codex-mock/snapshots/runs/nested-subagents-nowait\n    deviations:\n      - adr: capability-grounding\n        statement: >-\n          The statement's three layers and CLAUDE_CODE_MAX_SUBAGENT_SPAWN_DEPTH\n          are Claude Code's. Codex's depth limit is the config key\n          agents.max_depth, and its default is one layer: a\n          sub-agent cannot spawn its own until it is raised (recorded:\n          runs/nested-subagents with 3, runs/nested-subagents-limit with 2,\n          where the sub-agent at depth 2 found no spawn tool and said so). At\n          the limit the tool is not offered rather than a dispatch ending in an\n          error, and the mock answers a spawn_agent call there as the unknown\n          tool it is (\"unsupported call: spawn_agent\"). Where the depth and the\n          parent are recorded is the thread's own rollout meta record\n          (source.subagent.thread_spawn: parent_thread_id, depth), not a\n          sidecar, and all the session's rollouts, sub-agents' included, sit in\n          the one day directory under sessions/.\n      - adr: modeled-surface\n        statement: >-\n          The mock has no separate wait tool: its spawn_agent runs the\n          sub-agent to its end and answers with what a wait would, unless the\n          dispatch is the mock's own background one, which answers at once\n          with a receipt as Codex's spawn_agent does. Recorded, the main thread\n          spawned a sub-agent and ended the run without waiting for it, and\n          `codex exec` ended with the sub-agent still running, aborted\n          (runs/nested-subagents-nowait, turn_aborted); no recording has a\n          sub-agent leave its own sub-agents running. The wait tool's own\n          hooks (multi_agent_v1wait_agent) are not modeled.\n  cursor:\n    docs:\n      - https://cursor.com/docs/hooks#subagentstart\n    runs:\n      - cursor-mock/snapshots/runs/nested-subagents\n      - cursor-mock/snapshots/runs/nested-subagents-depth\n      - cursor-mock/snapshots/runs/nested-subagents-background\n    deviations:\n      - adr: capability-grounding\n        statement: >-\n          Cursor records neither a sub-agent's depth nor its parent: its\n          transcript is a file like the main agent's, agent-transcripts/<id>/<id>.jsonl\n          beside the others of the session (the one directory, as the statement\n          says), with no sidecar and no depth or parent field, and its hooks\n          report its own conversation id as their session (recorded:\n          runs/nested-subagents). The mock does the same.\n      - adr: capability-grounding\n        statement: >-\n          The statement's three layers and CLAUDE_CODE_MAX_SUBAGENT_SPAWN_DEPTH\n          are Claude Code's. Cursor's limit is two layers of sub-agents and has\n          no environment variable: a sub-agent of a sub-agent is not offered the Task tool\n          (it said no Task tool is available, runs/nested-subagents-depth),\n          rather than a dispatch ending in an error. The mock answers a Task\n          call there as an unknown tool and nests two layers.\n      - adr: modeled-surface\n        statement: >-\n          The Await tool, which the recorded main agent used to collect the\n          background sub-agent a sub-agent launched, is not implemented: the\n          mock's agents are scripts, and a session simply ends when the\n          background sub-agents it started are done. Recorded, the sub-agent\n          ended with its own report (STARTED) while the one it launched kept\n          running, and the run lasted until that one was done\n          (runs/nested-subagents-background).\n=======\n      - claude-mock/snapshots/runs/nested-fork-limit\n    deviations:\n      - adr: modeled-surface\n        statement: >-\n          A fork (the fork sub-agent type, on by default in interactive\n          sessions and opt-in with CLAUDE_CODE_FORK_SUBAGENT in print mode)\n          inherits the whole conversation and keeps its Agent tool at the\n          depth limit, where a dispatch is refused with an error. The mock\n          models a fork as the recorded run shows it, run in the background\n          with a sidecar of agentType fork, isFork and model inherit and\n          refused at the limit with the recorded error, and does not model\n          the inherited conversation or the fork-mode switch.\n  codex: pending\n  cursor: pending\n>>>>>>> bab62b52 (claude: tests/recordings for subagent-transcripts, nested-subagents, session-resume, session-fork, compaction-transcript-continuity)","is_error":false}]},"uuid":"330641b9-21b3-447a-87d1-4a8c8f58741c","timestamp":"2026-10-03T18:59:30.405Z","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"99ff2748-7a1f-4671-b08a-2a73a85f4d64","userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-desktop","cwd":"/Users/nsviridenko/ws/sloprail/harness-mocks/.claude/worktrees/agent-ab095323a3b