{"parentUuid":"b2ed83cf-d25e-4544-9cda-44f057802da9","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"0e75e1c2-9f84-43c4-8006-cccad7102c77","agentId":"ab095323a3b740c00","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01DZVkcig6g7KaXZSLPfqS4A","type":"tool_result","content":"the following rules refused this work:\n  - mock-config #1/#2 break: claude-mock/internal/runner/session_seed.go calls os.Getenv(EnvSessionName) (file is not in the ADR exceptions) and claude-mock/session_flags.go calls os.Setenv to smuggle --name to it; the ADR says \"N\no other code calls os.Getenv ... os.Setenv\" and flags are read once at the entrypoint into one configuration value passed down, so add a SessionName field to runner.Config set from the --name flag and have mockPreambleRecords use \ncfg. (file-guard \"adr-conformance\")\n  - The docs (sub-agents#let-subagents-spawn-their-own-subagents) say that in non-interactive mode a nested background sub-agent that finishes after its launcher ended 'reports to your main conversation instead', but TestT017_02f_\nLauncherDoesNotWaitForNestedBackground only asserts that a 'released' file exists (the launcher did not block). Nothing checks that the nested agent's task-notification and result reach the main conversation, so a mock that droppe\nd that report would still pass. Everything else is covered: spawnDepth/parentAgentId sidecars (T017_30), one subagents dir (T017_13), the default 3-layer limit and env override (T009_20/21), and the fork refusal error and hooks (T\n017_70/75).\n  - The CLI doc says --fork-session is used with --resume or --continue (cli-reference line 92), but no session-fork/claude test runs --continue --fork-session; every fork test uses --resume <id>, so the continue-then-fork variant\n is uncovered and no recorded run exists for it.\n  - Docs-stated behaviours have no test: `--no-session-persistence` (cli-reference: sessions are not saved and cannot be resumed) appears in no test and the mock does not model it; `--continue` is documented as loading the most re\ncent conversation in the *current directory*, but T017_74 uses one directory (its no-session case uses a separate empty config), so it never shows that a session from another directory is skipped; and T017_06 checks only the Sessi\nonStart transcript_path for the cross-directory resume, not the cwd and transcript_path that forkresume step 04 recorded on the later hooks (<RUN>/sub, projects/<RUN_DIRNAME>-sub/...a1.jsonl).\n  - claude-mock/internal/runner/runner_resume.go introduces a new token-accounting policy (`bytesPerToken = 4`, `cacheWriteUSDPerMillionTokens = 2.0`, `contextTokens = len(data)/bytesPerToken`), estimating token counts from transc\nript byte size, while the rest of the mocks report 0 tokens because 'the mock spends no tokens' (codex-mock/internal/events/stream.go:49) or take them from the scenario script (compaction PreTokens in claude-mock/internal/runner/r\necord.go:66); this makes the codebase disagree with itself on how a mock reports token counts and costs, and no ADR decides it: ask the user to decide it in a new ADR, or say which existing ADR it falls under. Every other choice i\ns covered: --name/--continue resolution and session_target.go fall under module internal/session, the env/flag handling under adr/mock-config, fork sidecar and spawn-limit result under module internal/subagents, and the compaction\n frame reorder under module internal/compaction. (file-guard \"concern-undeclared\")\n  - file-guard/config-at-entry (a mock reads its configuration once, at its entrypoint):\n- claude-mock/internal/runner/session_seed.go reads or writes the process environment: read it once at the entrypoint into the configuration\n- the code outside the allowed place now holds 13 sites, up from 12: legacy sites may only be removed (file-guard \"config-at-entry\")\n  - Home globs claim files of other concerns: claude-mock/internal/runner/runner_session_hooks.go (fireSessionStart/fireSessionEnd, hook context, prompt-blocked handling) is the hooks concern; claude-mock/internal/runner/session_s\need.go and session_append.go (appendToSession, preamble records, root-prompt writing) and codex-mock/internal/session/** (the append-only rollout File, TurnAborted, meta first record, sub.go sub-agent Origin) are the transcript (a\nppend-only record file) and subagents concerns, not finding/resuming/forking/id; narrow the globs or move these files to those modules.","is_error":false}]},"uuid":"a4284525-13ae-4f68-b1f2-f1fd23ed5854","timestamp":"2026-10-03T19:04:40.478Z","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"b2ed83cf-d25e-4544-9cda-44f057802da9","userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-desktop","cwd":"/Users/nsviridenko/ws/sloprail/harness-mocks/.claude/worktrees/agent-ab095323a3b740c00","sessionId":"f103aecd-8ff6-40a5-ad21-f5bd02338666","version":"2.1.286","gitBranch":"worktree-agent-a8a444ee54a52b4dc"}
