{"parentUuid":"9f0b7157-c9dc-4a68-b8d3-0baa673509b2","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"0e75e1c2-9f84-43c4-8006-cccad7102c77","agentId":"ab095323a3b740c00","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_0152xbuQP4My6BN4g6NDJzYT","type":"tool_result","content":"          The mock accepts -o/--output-last-message and does nothing with it:\n          the final message is not written to a file. It calls no model and\n          has no failing turn or stream failure, so the turn.failed event and\n          the stream-level error event the docs name are not modeled. The\n          stream's item types are the agent message and the command execution\n          only: reasoning, file changes, MCP tool calls, web searches and plan\n          updates are not modeled.\n      - adr: modeled-surface\n        statement: >-\n          Without --json the mock prints Codex's progress on stderr (banner with\n          release, directory, model and session; the prompt; the notices; each\n          command with how it ended and what it printed; the agent's message;\n          the tokens used, always 0), as recorded in\n          runs/noninteractive-run-text-output. It does not print the banner's\n          provider, approval, sandbox and reasoning lines, which are\n          configuration the mock does not have, the stdin notice, or a line per\n          hook run.\n      - adr: modeled-surface\n        statement: >-\n          The mock accepts --ephemeral and does nothing with it (it always\n          writes the session's rollout file), and reads no piped stdin: a\n          prompt argument plus piped input is not combined as additional\n          context.\n  cursor:\n    docs:\n      - https://cursor.com/docs/cli/headless#how-it-works","is_error":false}]},"uuid":"3f975ba8-9edb-43dd-87fb-f3e7e21f067d","timestamp":"2026-10-03T19:05:15.835Z","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"9f0b7157-c9dc-4a68-b8d3-0baa673509b2","userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-desktop","cwd":"/Users