{"parentUuid":"b18c0975-d53b-4723-8bdd-f1a2e1554eef","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"0e75e1c2-9f84-43c4-8006-cccad7102c77","agentId":"ab095323a3b740c00","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_014vA39xLAgr2Pi9EhgGJkpd","type":"tool_result","content":"sloprail: file-guard \"adr-conformance\" changeset: refused (19/26 settled, 2m23s)\nsloprail: file-guard \"capability-rigor\" session-resume: refused (23/26 settled, 2m42s)\nsloprail: file-guard \"capability-rigor\" session-fork: refused (25/26 settled, 2m48s)\nsloprail: file-guards evaluated in 3m2.584s (26 rules, concurrency 6)\nthe following rules refused this work:\nthe following rules refused this work:\n  - capability-once: internal/session/latest.go adds session-resume core behaviour (Latest picks the session --continue resumes; IDOfPath resolves a --resume path to an id) without the `// sr:capability session-resume` marker, tho\nugh the ADR says 'A capability's behaviour lives once, in `internal/`, on code marked `// sr:capability <id>`'; add the marker to Latest and IDOfPath, as find.go does for Find. (file-guard \"adr-conformance\")\n  - No test asserts that the fork's stream-json `init` and `result` frames carry the fork's new session_id. The Agent SDK sessions doc reads forkedId from the init message and `message.session_id` from the result, and forkresume/s\ntream.jsonl shows every b2 frame (init and result included) under b2. TestT017_77 only checks the `hook_started` `SessionStart:fork` frame, although its comment says it checks the init frame. The `--continue --fork-session` stream\n (T017_81) and the `--fork-session` plain-session stream are not checked at all. Everything else on the checklist is covered: source=fork with the new id, the history carried over, the original untouched, a plain `--fork-session` \nstarting as `startup`, and `--continue --fork-session`.\n  - runs/resume-name records session_title on the resume's UserPromptSubmit payload as well as SessionStart (