{"parentUuid":"3bf7a8e6-e9b1-4154-920b-91c611cb0ceb","isSidechain":true,"agentId":"ab095323a3b740c00","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011CffqnmcVCSimXWVwBNLfN","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01Q6qXNBxaktxK1Kpqins9g7","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"sed -n 1,12p internal/session/latest.go; sed -n 20,30p internal/session/find.go; cat adr/capability-once/ADR.md | sed -n 1,40p"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2287,"cache_read_input_tokens":404434,"output_tokens":560,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":86},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":2287},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":560,"cache_read_input_tokens":404434,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2287,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":2287,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"wireToolInputs":{"toolu_01Q6qXNBxaktxK1Kpqins9g7":{"command":"sed -n 1,12p internal/session/latest.go; sed -n 20,30p internal/session/find.go; cat adr/capability-once/ADR.md | sed -n 1,40p"}},"apiBlockIndex":2,"requestId":"req_011CffqnmH9TvNX4qBSXPp8q","attributionAgent":"general-purpose","type":"assistant","uuid":"63cf5024-e515-484a-9c2a-45e32e3f7ae6","timestamp":"2026-10-03T19:17:52.822Z","effort":"medium","perTurnEffort":"medium","userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-desktop","cwd":"/Users/nsviridenko/ws/sloprail/harness-mocks/.claude/worktrees/agent-ab095323a3b740c00","sessionId":"f103aecd-8ff6-40a5-ad21-f5bd02338666","version":"2.1.286","gitBranch":"worktree-agent-a8a444ee54a52b4dc"}
{"parentUuid":"63cf5024-e515-484a-9c2a-45e32e3f7ae6","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"0e75e1c2-9f84-43c4-8006-cccad7102c77","agentId":"ab095323a3b740c00","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01Q6qXNBxaktxK1Kpqins9g7","type":"tool_result","content":"package session\n\nimport (\n\t\"os\"\n\t\"path/filepath\"\n\t\"strings\"\n\n\t\"github.com/sloprail/harness-mocks/internal/transcript\"\n)\n\n// Latest is the id of the session a harness's `--continue` resumes: the most\n// recently written transcript of the project of cwd (the current directory's,\n// directory, else in any other project directory (a session begun in another\n// directory is resumed all the same); the most recently written wins when\n// several hold it. It is \"\" when none does, and for an id that is not a plain\n// file name.\n//\n// sr:capability session-resume\nfunc Find(l transcript.Layout, configDir, cwd, id string) string {\n\tif id == \"\" || strings.ContainsAny(id, `/\\`) || id == \".\" || id == \"..\" {\n\t\treturn \"\"\n\t}\n\tif p := l.FilePath(configDir, cwd, id); Exists(p) {\n---\nconcern: where a mocked harness capability is implemented, and how it is proven\nsloprails: [file-guard/shapes, file-guard/capability-covered, file-guard/capability-rigor, file-guard/adr-conformance]\n---\n\n# Each mocked capability is implemented once, in core\n\n## Concern\n\nHarness behaviour the mocks model: a Stop hook that blocks the turn, a\nPreToolUse refusal, compaction, background tasks, sub-agents. Several harnesses\nprovide the same capability with different wire formats.\n\n## Decision\n\n- `spec/capabilities/<id>.yaml` holds each capability the mocks model: a\n  harness-neutral statement, and for every harness mock one of: the doc\n  sections and recorded runs of that harness that show it (supported);\n  `{supported: false, reason, docs?, runs?}`, the evidence being recorded runs\n  that attempt the behaviour and show it absent and/or the doc sections that\n  show the feature absent or cover the area without it, at least one (a bare\n  `false` is not a cell: absence needs evidence); or `pending`: the harness mock has no adapter for\n  it. A `pending` cell does not block a merge and is never coverage;\n  `file-guard/capability-covered` lists every one on each run.\n- A capability's `<id>`, and so its file name, is kebab-case.\n- A capability's behaviour lives once, in `internal/`, on code marked\n  `// sr:capability <id>`.\n- A harness mock holds only its adapter: that harness's event names, payload\n  encoding and flags for the capability. Adapter code is marked\n  `// sr:provides <id>/<harness>`, and exists exactly for the supported\n  cells; a `pending` or unsupported cell has none. Any code under `<harness>-mock/` that affects a capability's\n  behaviour is that capability's adapter, marked or not.\n- An adapter translates and decides nothing: when a hook fires, whether a\n  block is honoured, and in what order things happen are the capability's.\n- Behaviour that differs between harnesses is a parameter of the core\n  capability, never a copy of it.\n- Every supported cell has tests, in `*_test.go`, marked\n  `// sr:proves <id>/<harness>`; the marker sits on tests only.\n- Those tests assert what the cell's recorded runs and docs show the real\n  harness doing, or the cell's declared deviation where the mock differs.","is_error":false}]},"uuid":"eb0b2c3a-618d-4062-b8b8-b7b4e8edbdba","timestamp":"2026-10-03T19:17:53.249Z","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"63cf5024-e515-484a-9c2a-45e32e3f7ae6","userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-desktop","cwd":"/Users/nsviridenko/ws/sloprail/harness-mocks/.claude/worktrees/agent-ab095323a3b740c00","sessionId":"f103aecd-8ff6-40a5-ad21-f5bd02338666","version":"2.1.286","gitBranch":"worktree-agent-a8a444ee54a52b4dc"}
