{"parentUuid":"cfc21ab0-2115-4336-a868-812224b2a40e","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"0e75e1c2-9f84-43c4-8006-cccad7102c77","agentId":"ab095323a3b740c00","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_017R3vP3Gd4yKLE1Umxzrswe","type":"tool_result","content":"sloprail: file-guard \"adr-conformance\" changeset: refused (23/27 settled, 1m35s)\nsloprail: file-guard \"capability-rigor\" hook-common-payload: refused (24/27 settled, 1m46s)\nsloprail: file-guard \"capability-rigor\" subagent-transcripts: refused (26/27 settled, 2m29s)\nsloprail: file-guard \"capability-rigor\" session-resume: refused (27/27 settled, 2m29s)\nsloprail: file-guards evaluated in 2m29.495s (26 rules, concurrency 6)\nthe following rules refused this work:\nthe following rules refused this work:\n  - capability-once: claude-mock/internal/runner/session_fork.go (ResumeTarget, LatestSession, newestSession, sessionTitleOf, ~lines 22-83) implements session-resume behaviour (choosing the session by name, by newest mtime for --c\nontinue) inside the harness mock, but the ADR says 'An adapter translates and decides nothing' and 'A capability's behaviour lives once, in internal/, on code marked // sr:capability <id>'; move the selection logic into the core i\nnternal/session package (marked sr:capability session-resume) and have the claude adapter only call it with its layout and flags. (file-guard \"adr-conformance\")\n  - The common-input-fields doc says that when running with `--agent`, every hook payload, main thread included, carries `agent_type` (the session's agent). No test drives this variant, the mock has no `--agent` flag, and the clau\nde provider declares no deviation for it. Add a test and a recording for it, or declare a deviation. The sub-agent and main-thread cases are otherwise covered (test_017_32 and test_017_03 for session_id, transcript_path, cwd, agen\nt_id and agent_type; test_009_03 for SubagentStart cwd).\n  - The resume-name run's stream records a `{\"type\":\"system\",\"subtype\":\"session_title_changed\",\"title\":\"earlier-by-name\"}` frame before init when a session is resumed by name, but no test asserts that frame (the string appears now\nhere outside the snapshots), and the deviations cover only the hooks' session_title, not this stream frame. Every other checklist item has a test: resume by id, by path, by name, --continue, no-session-persistence, resume from ano\nther directory, the resume SessionStart facts (the token ones asserted as 0, per the deviation), and no sub-agent hooks on resume.\n  - The sub-agents doc (Auto-compaction, sub-agents.md ~line 1126) says a sub-agent's own compaction is logged as a compact_boundary record in its own subagents/agent-<id>.jsonl transcript file, but no test drives a compaction ins\nide a sub-agent and asserts that record lands in the sub-agent's file and not the session's, and no <deviation> declares it unmodeled; test_017_subagent_files_persist_test.go only checks the session's compaction leaves sub-agent f\niles untouched.","is_error":false}]},"uuid":"d8ae01f5-37a7-4f87-9693-e288833908a3","timestamp":"2026-10-03T19:28:52.505Z","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"cfc21ab0-2115-4336-a868-812224b2a40e","userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-desktop","cwd":"/Users/nsviridenko/ws/sloprail/harness-mocks/.claude/worktrees/agent-ab095323a3b740c00","sessionId":"f103aecd-8ff6-40a5-ad21-f5bd02338666","version":"2.1.286","gitBranch":"worktree-agent-a8a444ee54a52b4dc"}
