{"parentUuid":"0f030390-735e-4fbd-bad1-756b89582315","isSidechain":true,"agentId":"ab095323a3b740c00","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011CfftAQpAvEU97C5wuteL9","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_014wUAHW4dFasYbYhsg3yEPU","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-nsviridenko-ws-sloprail-harness-mocks--claude-worktrees-harness-mocks-architecture-3031e7/f103aecd-8ff6-40a5-ad21-f5bd02338666/scratchpad/pr-body.md","content":"Pays the real gaps the judges flag on the claude pairs of subagent-transcripts, nested-subagents, session-resume, session-fork and compaction-transcript-continuity (plugin-hooks/claude re-judged clean).\n\nRecordings (claude 2.1.285, capture.sh): nested-fork-limit, transcript-retention, resume-continue, resume-continue-fork, resume-continue-none, resume-path, resume-name, no-session-persistence. capture.sh gains `@TRANSCRIPTS@` in a step's args (the folder the step's sessions are written to) so a run can resume by the path of a transcript.\n\nMock changes, each shown by a recording:\n- a compaction streams SessionStart:compact's hook frames inside the compaction window, before the end status, init and boundary\n- a fork (sub-agent type fork): background, sidecar agentType fork / isFork / model inherit, refused at the depth limit with the recorded error and a PostToolUseFailure\n- `--resume <path>`, `--resume <name>`, `--continue` (a new session when none), `--continue --fork-session`, `--no-session-persistence`; session_title on a named resume's SessionStart and the session_title_changed frame\n- the hooks after a resume's SessionStart from another directory are told the file really written\n- selection of the session to resume is in the session core (Target, Latest)\n\nTests (new files only) replay the meta, forkresume, compact, compact-nohooks and the new runs against the mock. Deviations declared only for parts the modeled-surface ADR covers (SendMessage sub-agent resume, fork-mode inheritance, --name, interactive resume parts, background sessions, tokens) and for the retention sweep a recording shows the real harness did not run.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":191,"cache_read_input_tokens":472029,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":191,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":14,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"wireToolInputs":{"toolu_014wUAHW4dFasYbYhsg3yEPU":{"file_path":"/private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-nsviridenko-ws-sloprail-harness-mocks--claude-worktrees-harness-mocks-architecture-3031e7/f103aecd-8ff6-40a5-ad21-f5bd02338666/scratchpad/pr-body.md","content":"Pays the real gaps the judges flag on the claude pairs of subagent-transcripts, nested-subagents, session-resume, session-fork and compaction-transcript-continuity (plugin-hooks/claude re-judged clean).\n\nRecordings (claude 2.1.285, capture.sh): nested-fork-limit, transcript-retention, resume-continue, resume-continue-fork, resume-continue-none, resume-path, resume-name, no-session-persistence. capture.sh gains `@TRANSCRIPTS@` in a step's args (the folder the step's sessions are written to) so a run can resume by the path of a transcript.\n\nMock changes, each shown by a recording:\n- a compaction streams SessionStart:compact's hook frames inside the compaction window, before the end status, init and boundary\n- a fork (sub-agent type fork): background, sidecar agentType fork / isFork / model inherit, refused at the depth limit with the recorded error and a PostToolUseFailure\n- `--resume <path>`, `--resume <name>`, `--continue` (a new session when none), `--continue --fork-session`, `--no-session-persistence`; session_title on a named resume's SessionStart and the session_title_changed frame\n- the hooks after a resume's SessionStart from another directory are told the file really written\n- selection of the session to resume is in the session core (Target, Latest)\n\nTests (new files only) replay the meta, forkresume, compact, compact-nohooks and the new runs against the mock. Deviations declared only for parts the modeled-surface ADR covers (SendMessage sub-agent resume, fork-mode inheritance, --name, interactive resume parts, background sessions, tokens) and for the retention sweep a recording shows the real harness did not run.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n"}},"apiBlockIndex":0,"requestId":"req_011CfftAQWq11WG1MQqf5yzK","attributionAgent":"general-purpose","type":"assistant","uuid":"c7852ebd-38ce-4e3d-9220-834197f012ab","timestamp":"2026-10-03T19:49:02.485Z","effort":"medium","perTurnEffort":"medium","userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-desktop","cwd":"/Users/nsviridenko/ws/sloprail/harness-mocks/.claude/worktrees/agent-ab095323a3b740c00","sessionId":"f103aecd-8ff6-40a5-ad21-f5bd02338666","version":"2.1.286","gitBranch":"worktree-agent-abb30e7cdc8998b15"}
