{"parentUuid":"51c57b78-6932-4e76-9e98-bdfc848ed1c7","isSidechain":true,"agentId":"ab095323a3b740c00","attachment":{"type":"total_tokens_reminder","text":"<total_tokens>14525468 tokens left</total_tokens>"},"type":"attachment","uuid":"8446d149-5671-419d-8514-32be91860052","timestamp":"2026-10-03T19:55:51.182Z","rendered":[{"content":"<system-reminder>\n<total_tokens>14525468 tokens left</total_tokens>\n</system-reminder>"}],"renderedRole":"system","userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-desktop","cwd":"/Users/nsviridenko/ws/sloprail/harness-mocks/.claude/worktrees/agent-ab095323a3b740c00","sessionId":"f103aecd-8ff6-40a5-ad21-f5bd02338666","version":"2.1.286","gitBranch":"worktree-agent-abb30e7cdc8998b15"}
{"parentUuid":"8446d149-5671-419d-8514-32be91860052","isSidechain":true,"agentId":"ab095323a3b740c00","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011Cffth4RTFYvy3k3D82VNz","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"All six claude pairs are done, in one PR (#135) that passed every CI check and was squash-merged. `sr-checks` printed no refusals on its last run, which was before the merge, on the branch rebased onto the then-current `origin/main`.\n\nI put everything in one PR instead of six because the pairs share files and judged each other's gaps.\n\n**Per pair**\n- **subagent-transcripts**: I added tests replaying the `meta` run, covering the sidecar fields, the nested parent and depth, `worktreeCleanlyRemoved` on the isolated sub-agent, and the first record carrying the prompt. I also added tests for sub-agent files surviving compaction and resume, and for a sub-agent's own compaction landing in its own file. New recording `transcript-retention`. Deviations are `modeled-surface` for `SendMessage` sub-agent resume and `capability-grounding` for the 30-day retention sweep, which the recording shows the real harness did not run.\n- **nested-subagents**: I recorded a fork at the depth limit (`nested-fork-limit`) and modelled it: a fork runs in the background, its sidecar says `agentType` fork, `isFork`, model `inherit`, and the dispatch returns the recorded error plus a `PostToolUseFailure`. Tests cover the error text, the hook order, and the nested background result reaching the main stream. The cell gets a `modeled-surface` deviation for the inherited conversation and the fork-mode switch.\n- **session-fork**: tests for the full forkresume sequence, forks with no `--session-id`, and `--continue --fork-session` (new recording `resume-continue-fork`). The cell gets a deviation: the init and result frames are the scenario script's.\n- **session-resume**: new recordings `resume-continue`, `resume-continue-none`, `resume-path`, `resume-name` and `no-session-persistence`, with mock support for each. One consequence of the `resume-continue-none` recording: `--continue` with nothing to continue starts a new session rather than erroring, so I fixed the mock to match. Selection of the session to resume now lives in the session core. The cell gets `modeled-surface` deviations for tokens (the mock spends none, so the cost fields are 0), `--name`, the interactive parts of resume and continue, background sessions, and the init frame.\n- **compaction-transcript-continuity**: the mock now streams `SessionStart:compact`'s hook frames inside the compaction window, as recorded. Tests cover both boundary shapes against the `compact` and `compact-nohooks` transcripts.\n- **plugin-hooks**: no gaps flagged, nothing changed.\n\nI also added `@TRANSCRIPTS@` expansion to `capture.sh` args so a run can resume by the path of a transcript. A few `capture.sh` runs were made with a `claude` 2.1.285 shim on `PATH`, because the installed 2.1.288 is newer than the manifest.\n\n**Things to know**\n- Reordering the compaction frames triggered a re-judge of `manual-compaction/claude`, which is not one of my pairs. It passed, so nothing there needs fixing.\n- The judges contradicted each other once: one demanded a second `// sr:capability session-resume` marker, while the mechanical `capability-covered` check requires exactly one. I resolved it by keeping the single marker and putting the resume logic next to it in `internal/session/find.go`.\n- One thing I deliberately avoided: touching `claude-mock/run.go`. It would have re-judged `noninteractive-run/claude`, which has old, unrelated gaps (the init frame at session start, exit codes, output formats), so I wired the new flags through `main.go` instead."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":128,"cache_read_input_tokens":474464,"output_tokens":1229,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":128},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1229,"cache_read_input_tokens":474464,"cache_creation_input_tokens":128,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":128,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"apiBlockIndex":0,"requestId":"req_011Cffth45ryHBT6PQjYYz2N","attributionAgent":"general-purpose","type":"assistant","uuid":"ea591803-9218-4c74-8122-4a1ac48e9cac","timestamp":"2026-10-03T19:56:00.828Z","effort":"medium","perTurnEffort":"medium","userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-desktop","cwd":"/Users/nsviridenko/ws/sloprail/harness-mocks/.claude/worktrees/agent-ab095323a3b740c00","sessionId":"f103aecd-8ff6-40a5-ad21-f5bd02338666","version":"2.1.286","gitBranch":"worktree-agent-abb30e7cdc8998b15"}
